  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-12-28T04:04:40.466Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The default laser direction for selecting menu items differs based on hardware, and is not a simple offset to even estimate from the player tracking data in Udon. Exposing a method that calculates and returns the direction and position from where the raycast originates will allow creators to easily script better custom interaction, such as simulating a pickup or interact. One use for this is on a chess board, instead of having a separate pickup for all 32 pieces, we could raycast from the players hand to find the nearest, and move a single pickup object to the found piece to \"pick up\" that piece, resulting in opportunities for optimization, or more natural interactions.",
